## Amethystora audit rules, key modules. amethystora-audit-home-rules copies this into
## /etc/audit/rules.d/60-amethystora.rules at every boot, before auditd starts, unless MODULES=off in
## /etc/amethystora/security.conf: a key that is off loads no rule and costs nothing. A watch on a path that
## is not there is left out, since it would stop auditctl loading every rule after it.
##
## Read what these caught with: sudo ausearch -i -k modules

## Loading a kernel module, by anyone who logged in. Modules the system loads for itself during boot
## are not attributable to a login (auid is unset) and would otherwise fill the log.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S init_module,finit_module,delete_module -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k modules
